module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.SmallSiteCoherenceOnSiteAgreement
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Coherence across `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a`, in the sense of Modules on Sites, Definition 03DL (8)

Let `S` be a scheme and `𝓕` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module.  Descent, Lemma 05VG says that the
equivalences `QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh((Sch/S)_τ, 𝒪)` and `QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh(S_τ, 𝒪)`, `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a`,
of Descent, Proposition 03DX preserve and reflect the properties of modules of Modules on Sites,
Definitions 03DE, 03DL and 03ER, except possibly "locally free" and "coherent".  For "coherent",
Definition 03DL (8), the source asserts the equivalence only for the small sites
`QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh(S_τ, 𝒪)` with `S` locally Noetherian and `τ ∈ {Zariski, étale}`.

Definition 03DL (8) on a ringed site `(𝒞, 𝒪)`: a sheaf of `𝒪`-modules `𝓖` is coherent if it is
of finite type and for every object `U` and every finite family of sections `s₁, …, sₙ` of `𝓖`
over `U` the kernel of `⊕ 𝒪_U ⟶ 𝓖|_U` is of finite type.  This is
`SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite`, and it is the predicate used on both sides below: on the left
for `𝓕` on the ringed site `(Opens(S), 𝒪_S)`, on the right for `𝓕^a` on the small site.

The ten sites of the lemma for this property:

* `(Sch/S)_Zar`: false, see the implementation notes; not stated.
* `(Sch/S)_étale`: false, see the implementation notes; not stated.
* `(Sch/S)_smooth`: false, see the implementation notes; not stated.
* `(Sch/S)_syntomic`: false, see the implementation notes; not stated.
* `(Sch/S)_fppf`: false, see the implementation notes; not stated.
* `S_Zar`: `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isCoherentOnSite_iff_smallZariskiAssociatedModule`
* `S_étale`: `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isCoherentOnSite_iff_smallEtaleAssociatedModule`
* `S_smooth`: false, see the implementation notes; not stated.
* `S_syntomic`: false, see the implementation notes; not stated.
* `S_fppf`: false, see the implementation notes; not stated.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isCoherentOnSite_iff_smallZariskiAssociatedModule`: for `S`
  locally Noetherian, `𝓕` is coherent if and only if `𝓕^a` is coherent on `S_Zar`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG.isCoherentOnSite_iff_smallEtaleAssociatedModule`: for `S`
  locally Noetherian, `𝓕` is coherent if and only if `𝓕^a` is coherent on `S_étale`.

## Implementation notes

Both statements follow the source's proof.  Over a locally Noetherian scheme, coherence of a
quasi-coherent module in the sense of 03DL (8) on `(Opens(S), 𝒪_S)` is coherence in the sense of
Stacks 01BV (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.isCoherentOnSite_iff_isCoherent`, by Stacks 01XZ),
and the latter is equivalent to 03DL (8) coherence of `𝓕^a` on the small site
(`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.isCoherentOnSite_associatedModule_iff` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isCoherentOnSite_associatedModule_iff`, which reduce to the finite
type and finite presentation cases and to coherence of the structure sheaf of the small site).

**The other eight sites.**  On the big sites `(Sch/S)_τ` for each of the five topologies, and on
the small sites `S_τ` for `τ ∈ {smooth, syntomic, fppf}` (the full subcategories
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite` of `(Sch/S)_τ` on the smooth, syntomic, respectively flat and
locally finitely presented `S`-schemes, with every `S`-morphism between them), the equivalence
fails already for `S = Spec k`, `k` a finite field (so that every scheme below is countable and
lies in every big site, whose size cutoff is uncountable), and `𝓕 = 𝒪_S`, which is coherent; so
these cells are not stated.  Namely, `𝓕^a = 𝒪` is not coherent on any of these sites.  Let
`U = 𝔸¹_k = Spec k[x]`, an object of each of them (it is smooth over `k`), and let `𝓚 ⊂ 𝒪_U` be the
kernel of multiplication by `x`, the sheaf of relations of the single section `x`, so
`𝓚(V) = {f ∈ Γ(V, 𝒪_V) ∣ x f = 0}` for `V ⟶ U`.  If `𝓚` were of finite type there would be a
covering `{Uᵢ ⟶ U}` with each `𝓚|_{Uᵢ}` generated by finitely many sections in `𝓚(Uᵢ)`.  Every
member of a Zariski, étale, smooth, syntomic or fppf covering is flat, and `x` is a nonzerodivisor
on `𝒪_U`, hence on `𝒪_{Uᵢ}`; so `𝓚(Uᵢ) = 0` and `𝓚|_{Uᵢ} = 0`.  But the origin `V = Spec k ⟶ U` is
an object of each of these sites (it is smooth over `k`), and the pullback of the covering to `V`
contains a nonempty `W ⟶ V` factoring through some `Uᵢ`; there `x` restricts to `0`, so
`𝓚(W) = Γ(W, 𝒪_W) ≠ 0`, a contradiction.  The small sites `S_Zar` and `S_étale` escape this
argument precisely because every morphism between their objects is an open immersion, respectively
étale, hence flat.  On the big fppf site this is the remark opening Stacks, Section 0GR4: the
category of coherent modules, in the sense of 03DL (8), on the big site of an algebraic stack is
zero, since the site contains too many objects that are not Noetherian, and coherent modules on
algebraic stacks are defined instead through Stacks 0GR5.

